Example gallery attribution
===========================

The Chart Studio example gallery is inspired by the R Graph Gallery:

  https://r-graph-gallery.com/
  Author: Yan Holtz and contributors
  Repository license: MIT
  https://github.com/holtzy/R-graph-gallery

The gallery does not redistribute images or text from the website.  Every
thumbnail in this directory was generated by RcmdrShiny Studio from the
bundled sample data with the same ggplot2 renderer used by the Chart Studio
preview.  The descriptions are original text.

Source pages used as inspiration for the first catalogue:

  https://r-graph-gallery.com/histogram.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/density-plot.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/boxplot.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/violin.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/beeswarm.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/ecdf.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/scatterplot.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/2d-density-chart.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/qq-plot.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/correlogram.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/heatmap.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/barplot.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/stacked-barplot.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/dotplot.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/pie-plot.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/line-plot.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/area-chart.html
  https://r-graph-gallery.com/time-series.html

The MIT license of the R Graph Gallery repository applies to its source code;
it does not grant rights to third-party images that may appear on the website.
For that reason this package ships only locally generated previews.
